  "comments": [
    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Verb(て) ＋ しまう。",
      "html": "Verb(て) ＋ しまう。",
      "credits_raw": "root1984",
      "content_sha256": "591e1c2e8b2f9b64fbb95c7be38dac865dddef17d79bf104a1ce362071a85055",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "It may be worth mentioning that sometimes \nVて　しまいました is sometimes shortened to \nVちゃった.",
      "html": "It may be worth mentioning that sometimes <br/>Vて　しまいました is sometimes shortened to <br/>Vちゃった.",
      "credits_raw": "agnestan",
      "content_sha256": "373a159fb77e8f016c81dc8221e890c86a8edc1bf838c6eda771353fb3e18b36",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Literally, しまう means \"to finish.\" Do not be surprised to find this word used only in this meaning sometimes, with no \"undesired\"-connotation.",
      "html": "Literally, しまう means \"to finish.\" Do not be surprised to find this word used only in this meaning sometimes, with no \"undesired\"-connotation.",
      "credits_raw": "blutorange",
      "content_sha256": "5959112f3137017070343f12e629a155729d7bf8206a67ea0cf2bf3bd8af0d47",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "-てしまう - sometimes contracted to ちゃう",
      "html": "-てしまう - sometimes contracted to ちゃう",
      "credits_raw": "lajka",
      "content_sha256": "a267f7bc8d71f607d0be965c267e271175477ded209dbcb1c1edb5d379911f66",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "The title should be \"shimau\" instead of \"teshimau.\" \"te\" is a particle and does not form the root of \"shimau.\"",
      "html": "The title should be \"shimau\" instead of \"teshimau.\" \"te\" is a particle and does not form the root of \"shimau.\"",
      "credits_raw": "bamboo4",
      "content_sha256": "2ee419ed612509ba85cfb9a85ee7fb12d53b5a3bda3b770b162e4410903b6b3c",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Wouldn't this fall under the other category of しまう？「その映画を見て泣いてしまった」にはほかの翻訳あると思いますが。。。 Watching that movie, I cried (not that I wanted to, or expected to cry). Perhaps because this would be a case where there isn't regret?",
      "html": "Wouldn't this fall under the other category of しまう？「その映画を見て泣いてしまった」にはほかの翻訳あると思いますが。。。 Watching that movie, I cried (not that I wanted to, or expected to cry). Perhaps because this would be a case where there isn't regret?",
      "credits_raw": "ninja_k",
      "content_sha256": "e566cef585a39701e0542359d452e017bd8fbc3ecfd5456b91f290631616502b",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "I think 〜てしまう can imply two meanings:\n1) completed\n2) to my regret\nI'm really not sure how one can distinguish which one a person is trying to imply.. I guess it's based on the context of what one is saying?",
      "html": "I think 〜てしまう can imply two meanings:<br/>1) completed<br/>2) to my regret<br/>I'm really not sure how one can distinguish which one a person is trying to imply.. I guess it's based on the context of what one is saying?",
      "credits_raw": "eastmael",
      "content_sha256": "51828a2dd9f1184f9edb2fefb929665bb0735ca6f4f8374902bb699fcbb0f9cc",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "I agree with eastmael. Here is some explanation from text :\n〜てしまう\n１．全部終わる\nE.g. : 作文をかいてしまったら、公園に行きましょう\n\n２．失敗する・残念だと思う\nE.g.: 1.大切な結婚指輪を無くしてしまいました。\n　　　2.大好きな猫が既に死んでしまったんだ。\n\nI think if something bad happened unwillingly, 〜しまう goes to the 2nd meaning.Otherwise, if it is something done without any special adverse effects or just a plain task or action, it goes to the 1st meaning.",
      "html": "I agree with eastmael. Here is some explanation from text :<br/>〜てしまう<br/>１．全部終わる<br/>E.g. : 作文をかいてしまったら、公園に行きましょう<br/><br/>２．失敗する・残念だと思う<br/>E.g.: 1.大切な結婚指輪を無くしてしまいました。<br/>　　　2.大好きな猫が既に死んでしまったんだ。<br/><br/>I think if something bad happened unwillingly, 〜しまう goes to the 2nd meaning.Otherwise, if it is something done without any special adverse effects or just a plain task or action, it goes to the 1st meaning.",
      "credits_raw": "誠",
      "content_sha256": "9ca3324b6d84cc3539fa34fde5651a25f527aea9472954dedb05a6342139bc31",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "I don`t know about everyone else, but I have never heard しまう used to mean \"I finished Ving\"\nIt always seems to have a negative meaning attached to it.",
      "html": "I don`t know about everyone else, but I have never heard しまう used to mean \"I finished Ving\"<br/>It always seems to have a negative meaning attached to it.",
      "credits_raw": "tigert",
      "content_sha256": "fe5943caf793016cb48f4ba00e609e8aa2bcedf284b69208badb1f002db2bc5d",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Tigertさん, I added example #6786 caught from JPLT2 in this level 3 entry exactly for the note you wrote.",
      "html": "Tigertさん, I added example #6786 caught from JPLT2 in this level 3 entry exactly for the note you wrote.",
      "credits_raw": "赤毛",
      "content_sha256": "c4ea77bcadea44c04b8624b54152901d653ddc1937ebdcfaab31805b3b0359cd",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 10,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "I'd like to offer a more natural translation of the sentence beginning with 前から欲しかった本。。。\n\nI got a book I had craved for a long time, so I immediately began reading, and read all night long until I finally finished it.",
      "html": "I'd like to offer a more natural translation of the sentence beginning with 前から欲しかった本。。。<br/><br/>I got a book I had craved for a long time, so I immediately began reading, and read all night long until I finally finished it.",
      "credits_raw": "kaligal",
      "content_sha256": "57423423eb325b73939176ab70125996bf4fe8966490f55eedaff3815d209401",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    }
  ],
